RELATIONAL DYNAMIC GEOMETRY  —  MANIFOLD COMPARISON NOTES

TYPE / OBJECT
  Independent TOE          : self-contained theory-of-everything class
  Theory-class             : grouping of users / models that share one TOE
  Knowledge manifold       : the geometric space of a whole domain
  Lower-dimensional manifold : reduced / projected slice of a domain
  Cross-class track        : comparison that stays unmerged

VARIABLES
  dim_L                    : dimension of the lower manifold
  dim_H                    : dimension of the reference / “whole” manifold
  lift(M_L → M_H)          : embedding / comparison map
  fractal_measure          : apparent roughness after lift
  domain_pair              : (philosophy | psychology)  vs  physics

FUNDAMENTALS
  1. Merging two independent TOEs is not an engineering gap.
     Segment first by theory-class; price and compare only inside a class.
     Keep a separate, non-merged track for any cross-class look.

  2. When you lift a lower-dimensional manifold onto a fuller one
     the lower slice looks fractal.
     Same pattern appears across knowledge domains:
       philosophy / psychology   compared with   the physics manifold.

  3. Relational Dynamic Geometry exists to perform those
     main-manifold comparisons without forcing everything
     onto a single shared scale.
